or, in general, \[a_n=(n-1)b+\frac{(n-2)(n-1)}{2}-(n-2)a.\] Note: we can easily prove this by induction. Now, substituting $n=19,92,$ we find that 
\begin{align*} 0=&18b+\frac{17\cdot18}{2}-17a\\ 0=&91b+\frac{90\cdot91}{2}-90a\\ b=&\frac{17a-\frac{17\cdot18}{2}}{18}=\frac{90a-\frac{90\cdot91}{2}}{91}. \end{align*}
Now, cross multiplying, we find that
