\begin{align*} x^2+(x+2)^2 &= 394\\ x^2+x^2+4x+4 &= 394\\ 2x^2 + 4x &= 390\\ x^2 + 2x &= 195\\ \end{align*}
From here, we can see that $x = 13$ as $13^2 + 26 = 195$, so there are $13$ girls, $13+2=15$ boys, and $13+15=\boxed{28}$ students.

