\begin{align*} r_1+r_2+r_3=-a \\ r_1+r_2+r_3+r_4=-1 \\ r_4=a-1 \end{align*}
The fourth root is $a-1$. Since $r_1$, $r_2$, and $r_3$ are common roots, we have:
